# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# X Lead Finder, example settings
#
# Copy this file to .env and paste your own keys in:
#
#     Windows:  copy .env.example .env
#     Mac/Linux: cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is listed in .gitignore, so it never reaches GitHub. This file
# has no real keys in it and is safe to share.
#
# No quotes, no spaces around the equals sign. Just key=value.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------


# --- Required -------------------------------------------------------

# The data supplier. Free starter credits on Google sign in, no card.
# Get it from https://twitterapi.io
TWITTER_API_KEY=paste_your_twitterapi_io_key_here

# The AI judge. Permanently free tier, no card required.
# Get it from https://aistudio.google.com
GEMINI_API_KEY=paste_your_google_ai_studio_key_here


# --- Optional, for the daily digest ---------------------------------
#
# Leave these out entirely and the digest still runs. It writes to
# data/digest.html and data/digest.txt instead of sending anything.

# Slack is the easiest. Create an app at https://api.slack.com/apps,
# turn on Incoming Webhooks, add one to a channel, paste the URL here.
# SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.slack.com/services/your/webhook/url

# Email, through any normal mailbox. Gmail needs an app password
# rather than your ordinary one. Port 465 for SSL, 587 for STARTTLS.
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
# SMTP_PORT=465
# SMTP_USER=you@example.com
# SMTP_PASS=your_app_password_not_your_login_password
# DIGEST_TO=where_the_digest_should_arrive@example.com
